Description: Fix generic icon shown for the running window in docks/taskbars
 The app-grid/launcher icon was already correct (desktop environments
 read that straight from mmassx.desktop's Icon= key), but the actual
 running window showed a generic icon in the dock/taskbar, with a
 tooltip literally reading "mmass.py" instead of "mMassX".
 .
 SetIcons() (called just above) only attaches icon pixel data to the
 window itself; it has no bearing on what identifies that window to a
 taskbar or dock. On GTK that's GLib's "prgname", and wx.App()
 unconditionally sets it to the running script's own filename,
 "mmass.py", overriding anything set beforehand (confirmed directly:
 a shell-level `exec -a` argv[0] override took effect at the process
 level but had zero effect here, since wx.App() overwrites prgname
 internally regardless of the process's real argv[0]).
 .
 Fix: explicitly re-set prgname after SetIcons(), which runs after
 wx.App() has already done its own (unwanted) assignment, confirmed
 directly:
 .
   prgname after wx.App():     b'-'
   prgname after mainFrame():  b'mmassx'
 .
 Uses ctypes against libgtk-3.so.0 directly rather than adding a
 PyGObject/gi dependency, since GTK is already a transitive runtime
 dependency of wxPython on Linux. Gated to __WXGTK__ and wrapped in a
 broad try/except since this is cosmetic (a wrong taskbar icon), not
 something that should ever be allowed to crash startup on some other
 GTK version or platform quirk.
Author: David <david@katalystnord.com>
Forwarded: https://github.com/SCIENCE-OPEN/mmassx/pull/2
Last-Update: 2026-09-08
--- a/gui/main_frame.py	2026-09-08 16:50:48.730005527 +0200
+++ b/gui/main_frame.py	2026-09-08 16:49:50.887170105 +0200
@@ -103,6 +103,22 @@
         icons.AddIcon(images.lib['icon128'])
         icons.AddIcon(images.lib['icon256'])
         self.SetIcons(icons)
+
+        # SetIcons above only attaches icon pixel data to this window; it
+        # has no effect on what identifies the window to a taskbar/dock,
+        # which on GTK is GLib's "prgname". wx.App() unconditionally sets
+        # that to the running script's own filename ("mmass.py"), so
+        # without this override every desktop environment's dock shows a
+        # generic icon and a "mmass.py" tooltip instead of matching this
+        # app to its .desktop entry.
+        if wx.Platform == '__WXGTK__':
+            try:
+                import ctypes
+                libgtk = ctypes.CDLL('libgtk-3.so.0')
+                libgtk.g_set_prgname.argtypes = [ctypes.c_char_p]
+                libgtk.g_set_prgname(b'mmassx')
+            except Exception:
+                pass
         
         # init basics
         self.documents = []
